cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use DENIS in your work, please cite it as below, and cite
  satlas2, clstools, and the CIAAW/AME mass tables for the underlying
  methods and data.
title: "DENIS: Doppler Estimation and Numerical Inference for Spectroscopy"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kayaalp
    given-names: Arda
    email: arda.kayaalp@kuleuven.be
    affiliation: KU Leuven
abstract: >-
  A desktop application for collinear laser spectroscopy (CLS):
  beam-time estimation, pre-analysis of ASDF runs, satlas2-based
  hyperfine-structure fitting, isotope-shift extraction with a
  Gaussian-process reference-drift correction, and results
  visualization.
keywords:
  - collinear laser spectroscopy
  - hyperfine structure
  - isotope shifts
  - nuclear structure
  - satlas2
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ardakayaalp/DENIS"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22081266
# ^ concept DOI (all versions); v1.0.0 is 10.5281/zenodo.22081267
